The module flag "Swift DirectReg Version" (1), as Xcode 27.0's frontend writes it after "Swift
Version" (ADR 0106, docs/formats/build.md "Swift runtime entry points by register"): for iOS, tvOS
and Mac Catalyst 17, watchOS 10 and visionOS, their simulators too, at every optimization level, and
never for macOS. Xcode's LLVM then calls the entry points that take their object in a given register
(swift_retain_x19 and the others) for the module's swift_retain and swift_release.

--- a/lib/IRGen/IRGen.cpp
+++ b/lib/IRGen/IRGen.cpp
@@ -206,6 +206,17 @@
   return std::make_tuple(TargetOpts, ClangOpts.CPU, ClangOpts.Features, ClangOpts.Triple);
 }
 
+/// Whether Xcode 27.0 marks the module for the Swift runtime entry points that
+/// take their object in a given register (swift_retain_x19 and the others):
+/// iOS, tvOS and Mac Catalyst 17, watchOS 10, visionOS, and their simulators.
+static bool usesDirectRegisterEntryPoints(const llvm::Triple &triple) {
+  if (triple.isiOS())
+    return triple.getiOSVersion() >= llvm::VersionTuple(17);
+  if (triple.isWatchOS())
+    return triple.getWatchOSVersion() >= llvm::VersionTuple(10);
+  return triple.isXROS();
+}
+
